Z||000000||NEO Cesek Racing||11-05-2001||07:15 PM||||ok i have two questions and hopefully someone can help me out tonight before i spend money on a part tomorrow. #1 i need to know how to get the rivets off the headlight motor to get at the two worn gears inside.  #2 can i just use tiny nuts and bolts to put the motor back together, i don't have a rivet gun.  i've already ordered the part i'm hoping if i get an answer before i have to go get it tomorrow i can do this myself and save some cashola.  thanks<P>------------------<BR>I used to have a handle <BR>on life but it broke.||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnF||11-05-2001||07:32 PM||||1.  What year of headlights do you have?  2.  From whom did you order the replacement parts?  <BR>3.  What parts have you ordered?<P>Help us out, here!||||reg||5
Z||000002||PBJ||11-05-2001||07:36 PM||||First you will need to drill the head of the rivit with a bit larger than the shaft of the rivit or grind it off. and yes you can just use a bolt and nut when you put it back together.||||reg||1
Z||000003||b52buf||11-05-2001||07:47 PM||||You have to drill out the old rivets.Use the smallest bit you can and still get the rivets out.As I remember it was 1/16th or 3/32 not absolutely sure which. Yes the unit can be put back together with screws and nuts. It would be smart to use self-locking nuts though. Also you should put some sealant in the grooves between the case halves.Just a thin line,don't get sealant in the mechanism. ||||reg||1
